<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11181" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrinna</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κόπιννα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A celebrated Greek poetess of Tanagra, contemporary
				with Pindar</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 3, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. S.
				5, 3, 158</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A feigned name of the object of the poet Ovid's
			love</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 2, 17, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 1,
			49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tr. 4, 10, 60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 8,
				73, 10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
